# Local AI/session artifacts — never repository documentation.
# These are scratch/log files from local development sessions and IM gateway
# operations. They are committed by accident; .gitignore rules prevent future
# tracking. Already-tracked instances are untracked via `git rm --cached`
# (file content remains on local disk).
Assisted.log
Notes.md
SESSION_STATE.md

# Local scratch/junk directory — never tracked.
# If a local .junk/ directory exists, it is disposable scratch material.
# Per SAAI rule: "archive/ preserves provenance; it is not a dumping ground."
# .junk/ contents are NOT archived; they are deleted locally when no longer
# needed. This rule prevents accidental tracking of disposable scratch.
.junk/

# IM gateway upload directory — never tracked.
# Per SAAI rule: this is the IM gateway's storage location for user-pasted
# content, not project content. Files here are disposable scratch from IM
# sessions and should never be committed. Preemptive rule (no files are
# currently tracked in upload/; this prevents future accidental tracking).
upload/
